1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,110
The old library here is a beautiful building isn't it wow really impressive.
这里的老图书馆是座美丽的建筑，不是吗？哇，真令人印象深刻。

2
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:12,910
I'm going to declare that that's arts and crafts and uh somebody can correct me in the comments.
我要判断它是工艺美术风格，有人可以在评论里纠正我；作者明确表示这只是自己的判断。

3
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:19,030
A fantastic timber framed building here look at that that's got some age on it.
这里有一座很棒的木框架建筑，看看它，真有些年头了。

4
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:24,750
I will endeavor to find out more and place that information on the screen.
我会努力查出更多信息，再把它放到屏幕上。

5
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:32,640
And st martin's church here that has a feel of a medieval church for sure wow.
这里是圣马丁教堂，确实有中世纪教堂的感觉，哇。

6
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:40,800
The church was possibly established in the late saxon period but the oldest parts of the building date from the 12 th century.
教堂可能在撒克逊晚期就建立了，但建筑现存最古老的部分来自十二世纪。

7
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:47,910
And that's the nave and the tower and it contains elements of roman brick and rubble.
那就是中殿和塔楼，里面也有罗马砖和碎石的构件。

8
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:59,310
The tower was damaged during the siege of colchester during the english civil war in 1648 and was never rebuilt.
塔楼在1648年英国内战中的科尔切斯特围城期间受损，此后再没重建。

9
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:09,790
So this seems to be the start of the dutch quarter here which was established in the tudor period by flemish uh refugees.
这里似乎就是荷兰区的起点，作者说它在都铎时期由佛兰芒难民建立。

10
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:17,560
A lot of them would have been weavers protestants fleeing persecution on the continent and establishing themselves here.
他们中很多大概是织工，是逃离欧洲大陆迫害、在此落脚的新教徒。

11
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:30,030
And a lot of the houses apparently do date from that tudor period from that 16 th century period obviously with some later development and alterations but already it's just wow.
很多房子显然来自都铎时期，也就是十六世纪，当然后来有扩建改动，但眼前已经让人惊叹。

12
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:42,960
So this house here it says in these houses lived jane and ann taylor authors and of original poems for infant minds 1796 to 1811.
这栋房子上写着，Jane 和 Ann Taylor 曾住在这些房屋，是《Original Poems for Infant Minds》的作者；字幕接着列1796至1811年。

13
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:50,310
I wonder if that is twinkle twinkle little star someone composed it in the dutch quarter.
我在想那是不是《小星星》，有人就是在荷兰区写的；作者并未确定对应关系。

14
00:01:50,320 --> 00:02:22,670
These are really fascinating houses aren't they this would be a reason to come to colchester on its own just to look at these dutch dwellings from the 16 th century.
这些房子太有意思了，单是看这些十六世纪的荷兰式住宅，就值得来科尔切斯特。

15
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:32,110
Wat tyler walk of course wat tyler being a man of essex leader of the peasants revolt of 1381.
Wat Tyler Walk；当然沃特·泰勒是埃塞克斯人，是1381年农民起义的领袖，作者这样介绍。

16
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:49,870
This is north gate and I think if we carry on down here along north gate we get to the castle park and what I think is the heart of roman colchester.
这里是 North Gate；我想沿着它继续走，就会到城堡公园，也就是我认为的罗马科尔切斯特中心。

17
00:02:49,880 --> 00:03:01,470
So let's enter into castle park via rye gate and here we have another quite substantial section of roman wall.
我们经由 Rye Gate 进入城堡公园，这里又有相当大一段罗马城墙。

18
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:07,790
And the romans built their city I think in what's now the upper park or part of their city.
我想罗马人把城市，或者城市的一部分，建在现在的上层公园。

19
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:20,470
There was a temple of claudius upon this hill that we will ascend and think of boudica destroying it.
我们将登上的山丘曾有克劳狄乌斯神庙，想到布狄卡摧毁它的情景；历史依作者讲述。

20
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:29,510
So close by to here was one of the roman watchtowers that were built along the wall rising high above looking out.
附近曾有一座罗马瞭望塔，沿城墙修建，高高耸立，向外观察。

21
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:37,860
I mean did they see boudica coming or not and this is the oldest surviving roman town wall in England.
我的意思是，他们到底有没有看见布狄卡过来？而这就是英格兰现存最古老的罗马城镇城墙，作者这样介绍。
